The limit on the virtual memory, the address space, a process of the container can use (unit byte).
Same as `limit_as`: when both are set, the larger value is used.

The engine sets the soft and the hard limit to this value, as `--ulimit
as=<value>:<value>`, which overrides its default ulimit and the `--ulimit as`
of `run_args`. Unset, the container runs with the default of the engine.
